{"title":"Control Systems Engineer Roadmap","role":"Control Systems Engineer","summary":"An EEE degree is strongly aligned with control systems engineering. The field combines electrical systems, electronics, mathematics, signal processing, instrumentation, programming and automation to design systems that monitor, regulate and control physical processes.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 of UG","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Timeline assumption":"Four-year B.Tech/B.E. beginning in 2026 and graduating around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Control Systems Engineer is a realistic graduate-entry career. Common entry routes include Graduate Engineer Trainee, Control Engineer, Automation Engineer, Instrumentation Engineer, PLC/SCADA Engineer and Electrical Systems Engineer."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"automation, controls, instrumentation, PLC/SCADA, robotics and electrical engineering internships"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"industrial control, PLC/SCADA, robotics, motion control, embedded control or process automation"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"control-system architecture, automation leadership, safety systems and advanced process optimisation"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"autonomous control, AI-assisted optimisation, digital twins, industrial IoT and intelligent automation"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An EEE degree is strongly aligned with control systems engineering. The field combines electrical systems, electronics, mathematics, signal processing, instrumentation, programming and automation to design systems that monitor, regulate and control physical processes."},{"type":"p","text":"Control Systems Engineers work across industrial automation, robotics, manufacturing, power systems, automotive, aerospace, process industries and embedded systems."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 · Sem 1"},{"text":"C/Python, engineering mathematics, basic electrical circuits"},{"text":"Python documentation · MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/"},{"text":"Programming and circuit-analysis exercises"},{"text":"Digital literacy"}],[{"text":"Year 1 · Sem 2"},{"text":"Signals and systems, electronics and measurement fundamentals"},{"text":"NPTEL","url":"https://nptel.ac.in/"},{"text":"Signal-processing simulations"},{"text":"Analytical thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 2 · Sem 1"},{"text":"Control theory, transfer functions, feedback and stability"},{"text":"MIT OpenCourseWare","url":"https://ocw.mit.edu/"},{"text":"MATLAB/Python control-system simulations"},{"text":"Technical reasoning"}],[{"text":"Year 2 · Sem 2"},{"text":"Sensors, actuators, microcontrollers and embedded programming"},{"text":"Arduino · Raspberry Pi","url":"https://www.arduino.cc/"},{"text":"Closed-loop temperature/motor-control project"},{"text":"Execution"}],[{"text":"Year 3 · Sem 1"},{"text":"PLC, SCADA, industrial networking and automation"},{"text":"Siemens Automation","url":"https://www.siemens.com/global/en/products/automation.html"},{"text":"PLC/SCADA simulation project"},{"text":"Systems thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 3 · Sem 2"},{"text":"PID tuning, state-space control, motor drives and robotics"},{"text":"ROS 2 documentation","url":"https://docs.ros.org/"},{"text":"Robotic or motor-control project"},{"text":"Problem solving"}],[{"text":"Year 4 · Sem 1"},{"text":"Advanced control, digital twins, industrial IoT and safety"},{"text":"MathWorks Control Systems","url":"https://www.mathworks.com/products/control.html"},{"text":"Digital-twin/control simulation"},{"text":"Strategic thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 4 · Sem 2"},{